  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0067_9c2d22b3d869.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 153px;\" /></p><p>The aeroplane imparts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> velocity to the food packet horizontally when dropping. Horizontal range of food packet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math><br />Also, Horizontal distance, travelled by aeroplane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">v</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math> thus, vertical distance between aeroplane and person <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math><br />distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
